# SchoolPilot crontab for the `schoolpilot` cPanel user.
#
# Install with:  crontab -u schoolpilot deploy/cpanel/cron/schoolpilot.cron
# Verify with:   crontab -u schoolpilot -l
#
# You can also paste these into cPanel > Cron Jobs, but keeping them in the
# repo means the next person to rebuild this box gets them.

MAILTO=ops@schoolpilot.org.ng
PATH=/opt/cpanel/ea-php82/root/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# --- Laravel scheduler -----------------------------------------------------
#
# One entry, every minute, forever. Laravel decides internally which of the
# commands in routes/console.php are due. This single line is what runs
# cbt:expire-attempts, id-cards:sweep and exports:sweep.
#
# cbt:expire-attempts is the one that hurts if this is missing: it closes CBT
# attempts whose time has run out. Without the scheduler an exam never ends on
# its own, and the failure is invisible until a student's paper stays open.
* * * * * cd /home/schoolpilot/current/backend && php artisan schedule:run >> /home/schoolpilot/logs/schedule.log 2>&1

# --- Nightly database backup (LAUNCH.md §2) --------------------------------
#
# WHM's own backups cover MySQL. Postgres was installed outside cPanel's
# management, so cPanel does not know it exists and will not back it up. If
# this line is missing you have a backup policy on paper and no backups.
#
# 02:00 UTC = 03:00 WAT, per LAUNCH.md. RPO is 1 hour, which a nightly dump
# alone does not meet — enable Postgres WAL archiving as well before the RPO
# claim is true.
0 2 * * * /home/schoolpilot/current/deploy/cpanel/backup-db.sh >> /home/schoolpilot/logs/backup.log 2>&1

# --- Log rotation guard ----------------------------------------------------
#
# Laravel is on the `single` channel by default (LOG_STACK=single), which
# never rotates. On a school-hours traffic pattern that file reaches gigabytes
# and fills the partition, which takes down Postgres before it takes down PHP.
# Set LOG_CHANNEL=daily in .env as well; this is the cleanup for it.
30 3 * * * find /home/schoolpilot/current/backend/storage/logs -name '*.log' -mtime +14 -delete
